  "market_context": "During a strong uptrend in GER40, a regular bearish divergence formed on the 15-minute chart: price made a higher high while RSI made a lower high. Price briefly corrected downward but then resumed a strong rally, invalidating the divergence signal.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst highlighted that although price formed a higher high and RSI a lower high (classic regular divergence), price did not reverse but instead continued significantly higher, demonstrating unreliability of LTF divergences for swing trades.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a higher high in price on the GER40 15-minute chart.",
    "Step 2: Observed a corresponding lower high in the RSI indicator, forming a regular divergence.",
    "Step 3: Noted that price initially dropped after the divergence but then rallied strongly higher, invalidating the reversal signal.",
    "Step 4: Contrasted this with higher-timeframe Bitcoin daily chart divergences to emphasize that only HTF divergences carry reliable weight for swing trades."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Regular divergences on lower time frames (e.g., 15m) can fail during strong trends; rely on higher time frame divergences (e.g., daily) for higher-probability swing trade entries.",
